DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iitthheerrmm driver provides support for several sensors found in Intel
     3400 and 5 series chipsets.

     The sensors currently exposed via the sysctl(8) interface are:

           SSeennssoorr             UUnniittss    TTyyppiiccaall UUssee
           Thermometer        degC     Temperature
           Core 1             degC     Temperature
           Core 2             degC     Temperature
           CPU power cons.    Watts    Power usage
           CPU/GPU Max        degC     Temperature
           DIMM 1             degC     Temperature
           DIMM 2             degC     Temperature
           DIMM 3             degC     Temperature
           DIMM 4             degC     Temperature
           GPU abs.           degC     Temperature
           PCH abs.           degC     Temperature

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     pci(4), sensorsd(8), sysctl(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The iitthheerrmm driver first appeared in OpenBSD 4.8.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The iitthheerrmm driver was written by Mike Larkin <_m_l_a_r_k_i_n_@_o_p_e_n_b_s_d_._o_r_g>.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     Not all sensors are wired on every machine, so the list of sensors shown
     in sysctl(8) may not show all the sensors listed above.  Furthermore, the
     iitthheerrmm driver will flag sensors as invalid if they report bogus data.

